AI, Machine Learning, and IoT/Edge in Azure

1. Artificial Intelligence (AI)

AI in Azure allows apps to perform tasks that normally require human intelligence (like vision, speech, decision-making).

Use prebuilt services — no deep coding needed
Examples:
          Vision (image recognition)
          Speech (speech-to-text)
          Language (text analysis, chatbots)
Good for adding “smart” features quickly

2. Machine Learning (ML)

Machine Learning is a subset of AI where systems learn from data and improve over time.

Build, train, and deploy models
Works with large datasets
Requires more control than basic AI services
Main service:
              Azure Machine Learning
Used for predictions (e.g. sales forecasting, fraud detection)

3. IoT / Edge

IoT (Internet of Things) connects physical devices to the cloud.

Devices send and receive data (e.g. sensors, machines)
Azure collects, monitors, and analyzes this data

Edge computing processes data closer to the device instead of the cloud

Faster response
Works even with limited internet
Key services:
              IoT Hub (device management)
              IoT Edge (run workloads on devices)
